# MHC window on the CHM13v2.0 (T2T) primary assembly (DESIGN.md S3.1).
#
# CORRECTED 2026-08-31, user-directed, real HG03583 ONT benchmark: the
# window below (chr6:1,214,347-4,666,036) was wrong -- confirmed directly,
# a real sample's reads with 55x true depth sitting exactly on HLA-A's own
# real coordinates produced zero anchor alignment, and the region as a
# whole recruited essentially nothing (0 reads kept by the Stage 0 sieve
# out of 26,598 extracted). The old window was derived from this
# workspace's pre-existing hla_genes.bed (one directory up from hlaont/,
# "confirmed with the user, not independently re-derived" per the
# 2026-07-21 session that first wrote this file) -- that trust was
# misplaced; hla_genes.bed's own CHM13 coordinates do not correspond to
# where the MHC locus actually sits on this real chr6. The real window,
# user-supplied and directly correct on the real sample: chr6:28,385,000-
# 33,500,000 -- notably close to GRCh38's own MHC window position
# (chr6:28,510,120-33,480,577, mhc_window.grch38.bed), consistent with
# CHM13v2.0 and GRCh38 placing the MHC locus at a similar absolute
# chromosome position, unlike what the old, wrong window implied.
#
# chr6 length verified independently: 172,126,628bp, matching both the
# local CHM13_0_chr6.fasta.fai and UCSC's hs1.chrom.sizes -- this part
# was correct and unaffected by the fix above (build detection itself,
# input/regions.py's derive_regions(), was never the bug).
#
# 0-based half-open BED coordinates.
chr6	28385000	33500000	MHC_window
